Projects/UOContent/Misc/Titles.cs

Adds an overload of Titles.GetSkillTitle that takes the skill to title by, instead of always reading the
mobile's own highest. The old signature stays and now calls the new one with GetHighestSkill(mob), so every
caller in the engine gets exactly what it got before. Without this patch BotAIv2 does not compile.

WHY. Every bot is handed some skills at birth as a matter of course, and a granted skill is not an
achievement: within the hour of Item Identification being handed out on 08.09.2026 the whole population read
"Grandmaster Merchant". A bot's rank is the title of the best skill it worked up to itself — see Rank and
Earned in Projects/BotAIv2/BotPopulation/BotMobile.cs — and the dashboard shows it as "Name, Rank".

Mobile.Title is left alone on purpose. To this engine it is the custom title: AddNameProperties glues it to
the name with a bare space, and Titles.ComputeTitle takes a non-empty Title as a signal to skip the skill-title
branch, which is the one that writes the comma. Writing the rank there spoiled the name and switched off the
code that would have got it right.

